From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0317-lichii-shaders-0203-query-dma-trace-and-sync.patch

Source: 0317-lichii-shaders-0203-query-dma-trace-and-sync.patch
Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches as 0203.

Port of zortos293/Lichii ea05503e5 (the EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_TRACE commit of PR 150, in f26ad432a)
and 0c0a2e0e6 (EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_SYNC, branch test/all-in-one-flash, marked as an experiment
there), both zortos293.

Lichii's PR 150 says macro 0x142 read a stale "visible" record, ran its half-res depth clears every
frame and drew the fog over Link and the terrain. fog-04 ports that flush, but it does nothing
under the split, and Ocarina on the console runs the split. The split read waits for no report:
below High accuracy a counter report reaches guest memory when a later fence pops. Whether that
bites here is not known. This patch makes it visible and testable:

EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_TRACE=1 logs each macro DMA read of a report still pending, with the words read,
then the same words once they landed (capped at 4000). Different words mean a stale read. Equal
words mean nothing: "pending" here is "still registered in the query cache" (nothing sets
IsGuestSynced), so a report that landed a moment ago is logged too. No lines at all only clears
long reports: short ones (IsAFence) are never registered below High, they are written at once.
EDEN_NX2_QUERY_DMA_SYNC=1 also blocks at such a read until a new fence has popped, reports already
landed included. Expect it to cost frames. Its wait is new on the console: WaitPendingFences never
really waits at Low accuracy (SignalFence runs its function at once), so that path proves nothing.

With lichii-gpu-0215's EDEN_NX2_DMA_WAIT_WRITERS set, a read can return before this hook: leave it
unset for these tests.

Changed from the source: split path only, in FrontDmaRead's Defer on the back; macro.cpp is left to
fog-04. SignalAndWait also calls SubmitDeferredWork, as WaitPendingFences does here (0141), or the
back would wait for a fence that needs its own submission.

Both default off; unset, nothing changes. Memory: none. Not run. Syntax checked with clang only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

